   track       : ratified
   history     : Multi-Active SCD2
   feeders     : 1 emitted of 1 (one per source view AND run)
   runs        : 1 -- opus_health_legacy_v4
   payload     : 3 attribute(s), NULL-PADDED TO THE SATELLITE
   grain       : ONE ROW PER HUB_FINANCIAL_TRANSACTION_HK
   hashdiff    : SAT_FINTXN_RECON_INSTRUMENT_HASHDIFF (builder decision BD1), GUARDED against an all-null input (s5.5):
                 without the guard every all-null row hashes to ONE value and the
                 satellite collapses to one row, which looks like change detection.
   child key declared by data_7.js: 'Instrument Sequence'
   REFUSED, DECLARED, NOT GUESSED -- view BJAZ_HEALTH_WEBSERVICE_INFO (opus_health_legacy_v4), sub-population leg_and_value:
     legs ['Instrument Sequence'] are NAMED CORRECTLY and the value answers a DIFFERENT
     QUESTION. SAT_FINTXN_RECON_INSTRUMENT declares 'Instrument Sequence' and the map
     supplies 'Instrument Sequence = {INSTR_NUMBER}' -- the leg naming is right, the VALUE
     is the wrong KIND, which is why relabelling cannot fix it. Refused, not coined.
     discriminator states found: {'child_key': 'POPULATED', 'child_key_value': 'POPULATED', 'child_key_components': 'ABSENT', 'usage_child_key': 'ABSENT', 'key_name': 'PRESENT_NULL', 'instance': 'PRESENT_NULL'}
   CONSEQUENCE, stated because it is not recoverable after load: rows differing ONLY
   in a refused leg COLLAPSE onto one hash key. The collapse is DECLARED and
